PXL
----

Minimal 2D graphics library in C99.

Features:
  - 2D primitives: line, rect, circle, triangle (outline + filled)
  - Canvas with scissor clipping, translation offset, color, clear, blit
  - Test outputting using either built-in 8x8 ascii font or monospace or
    proportional bitmask font
  - Backends: SDL2, X11 (uses SHM, XIM/XIC extensions for performance and UTF-8 input)
  - Keyboard/mouse input

Build:
  make          # Build libpxl.a (default backend: x11)
  make BACKEND=sdl  # Build with SDL2 backend
  make lint     # Static analysis with strict warnings (-Werror)
  make test     # Run unit tests (default backend)
  make demo     # Build demos
  make clean    # Remove build artifacts

  Build configuration:
    Main configuration is defined in Makefile.inc.
    Copy 'config.mk.example' to 'config.mk' to override backend, CFLAGS, or library paths.
    Use 'sh test-all.sh' to test all backends (x11, sdl) and tools.

Quick start:
    /* Minimal PXL application */
    pxl_app_t app = {
        .title = "My App",
        .width = 800,
        .height = 600
    };

    if (pxl_app_init(&app) != PXL_SUCCESS) return 1;

    while (pxl_app_advance_wait(&app)) {
        if (pxl_app_was_pressed(&app, PXL_KEYB_ESCAPE)) break;

        pxl_buf_t pb;
        if (pxl_backend_begin_frame(&pb) == PXL_SUCCESS) {
            pxl_canvas_t cnv;
            pxl_canvas_init(&cnv, &pb);
            pxl_canvas_clear(&cnv);

            /* Draw here */
            pxl_draw_str(&cnv, 100, 100, "Hello, PXL!");

            (void)pxl_backend_end_frame();
        }
    }

    pxl_app_deinit(&app);

    /* For games with physics/stepper: see demo_pong.c */

Demos:
  - demo_hello_world.c - Minimal example: static drawing (colored rect + text)
  - demo_pong.c        - Complete game: physics, input, rendering, interpolation
  - demo_gas.c         - Particle simulation with stats
  - demo_typewriter.c  - Text rendering and animation
  - demo_fountain.c    - Sprite and tileset usage


Architecture:
  Core:
    err.h          - Error codes
    buf.h          - uint32_t pixel buffer with stride alignment
    input.h        - Input state handling (keyboard, mouse, window events)
    backend.h      - Backend interface. All backends use ARGB8888 pixel format
                     (A:24-31, R:16-23, G:8-15, B:0-7).

  Backend:
    backend_sdl.c - SDL2 backend (do not activate VSYNC)
    backend_x11.c - X11 backend (uses SHM, XIC extensions for performance)

  Gfx:
    bitmask.h      - 1-bit per pixel mask for stencil/clip operations
    color.h        - ARGB8888 color creation and component extraction
    canvas.h       - Drawing surface with color, scissor, translation offset, clear, blit
    camera.h       - Offset-based camera management helpers
    geom.h         - Geometry primitives (rect, span) and clipping
    blit.h/c       - Pixel operations (blit, bitmask drawing)
    shape.h/c      - 2D primitives (line, rect, circle, triangle, outline + filled)
    text_basic.h/c - ASCII text rendering with built-in 8x8 font (char, string, bounds)

  Framework:
    app.h          - Optional app layer: frame management, input, poll/wait event modes
    stepper.h      - Time-stepped physics loop helper (fixed timestep, interpolation)
    text.h/text.c  - Text rendering with mono or proportional LSB bitmask font
    tileset.h/c    - Tile rendering: grid atlas (tileset) + animation frames (sprite)

  pxl.h - umbrella header that includes all public headers. For finer
          granularity, users may include individual headers directly.

Tools:
  - bdf2pxl - Convert BDF font files to pxl_font_t C header
    Example: bdf2pxl -n my_font -r U+0020-U+007F DejaVuSans.bdf > my_font.h

Testing:
  Framework: test.h (minimalist assert-based testing)
  Run tests: make test or sh test-all.sh to go through all available backends.

